### star-proj-adopt/references/adopt_spec.md
--- 1
Six areas, each with a confidence: `certain` (one unambiguous match), `likely` (one match, weak signal), `unknown` (none or several). Only `likely` and `unknown` lines reach Confirmation point 1; a `certain` line is reported, not asked about. Because that label decides what is asked, the main agent sets it: an area handed to a subagent comes back with findings and evidence paths and an empty confidence column, so the subagent never decides what the user gets asked about.
+++ 1
Six areas, each with a confidence: `certain` (one unambiguous match), `likely` (one match, weak signal), `unknown` (none or several). Only `likely` and `unknown` lines reach Confirmation point 1; a `certain` line is reported, not asked about. Because that label decides what is asked, the main agent sets it: an area handed to a collection pass comes back with findings and evidence paths and an empty confidence column, so the collection pass never decides what the user gets asked about.
### star-proj-adopt/references/adopt_spec_zh.md
